 - 1 pm at the 12th Street and Piedmont Avenue Gate. We can\'t wait to celebrate with you!',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/green-market-15th-anniversary-celebration',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:11','2019-09-21 01:17:11'),(1618,'Art On The Atlanta Beltline Lantern Parade','art-on-the-atlanta-beltline-lantern-parade-september-21-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-09-21',NULL,'N/A','7:00 PM','10:00 PM','On Saturday, September 21st, starting at 7:00 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Atlanta BeltLine, Inc. \nChris Langley -clangley@atlbeltline.org \nEVENT DESCRIPTION: Evening Community Event with LED-Lit lanterns marching on the BeltLine. \nLOCATION/ROUTE: The Atlanta BeltLine East Side beginning at Irwin St and Krog St. to travel to Monroe Dr/Piedmont Park along the BeltLine Trail. \n*EVENT PENDING PERMIT*',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/city-permit-art-on-the-atlanta-beltline-lantern-parade',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:14','2019-09-21 01:17:14'),(1619,'Free Workout: Hiit (High Intensity Interval Training) With Northside Hospital','free-workout-hiit-high-intensity-interval-training-with-northside-hospital-september-28-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-09-28',NULL,'Free','8:00 AM','9:00 AM','On Saturday, September 28th, starting at 8:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join Piedmont Park Conservancy Sponsor Northside Hospital at the Active Oval for a free high-intensity interval exercise program. Make sure to bring a water bottle, mat and get ready to sweat \n\n\n\nSaturday, September 28\nSaturday, October 26\n\n\n\nTime: 8am-9am \nLocation: Piedmont Park - North Soccer Field 2 at the Active Oval \nBenefits include: \n\n\n\nFast results\nFat Loss\nMuscle tone\nCardio\n\n\n\nLearn more about Northside Hospital at: sportsmedicine.northside.com',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/free-workout-hiit-high-intensity-interval-training-with-northside-hospital-2/2019-09-28',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:22','2019-09-21 01:17:22'),(1620,'Atlanta Audubon Society Chalk Art Festival','atlanta-audubon-society-chalk-art-festival-september-29-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-09-29',NULL,'N/A','1:00 PM','6:00 PM','On Sunday, September 29th, starting at 1:00 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Make Piedmont Park your canvas during Atlanta Audubon\'s Chalk Art Festival as part ofGeorgia Grows Native for Birds Month this September! We invite families, individuals, non-profits, businesses, corporate partners, and localartiststo create temporary drawings which will brighten the unveiling following thefestival.Participants will receive a square in which to create a unique work of art celebrating Georgia\'s native plants and animals. The event will take place in front ofAtlanta Audubon\'s Exhibitat at Piedmont Park. Proceeds from the Chalk Art Festival will fund Chimney Swift tower construction projects in the metro area.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/city-permit-atlanta-audubon-society-chalk-art-festival',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:25','2019-09-21 01:17:25'),(1621,'Members\' Tree Tour','members-tree-tour-october-15-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-10-15',NULL,'N/A','5:30 PM','7:00 PM','On Tuesday, October 15th, starting at 5:30 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join us for a unique members\' event with special guest Steve Sanchez, Principal with HGOR. \nThe tour will highlight the diversity of tree species found in Piedmont Park, focusing on their importance to the health of our urban ecology. Topics of discussion will include: \n\nThe species that are proving to be the toughest survivors in our urban environments\nThe importance of native trees and their importance to wildlife.\nHow trees help to mitigate stormwater and the urban heat island\nFall color, flowers and form: What are the aesthetic qualities of our park trees?\n\nSpace is limited, so please RSVP to hreed@piedmontpark.org as soon as possible.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/members-tree-tour',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:29','2019-09-21 01:17:29'),(1622,'Moving Day Atlanta','moving-day-atlanta-october-19-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-10-19',NULL,'N/A','9:00 AM','12:00 PM','Celeste Tennant \nctennant@parkinson.org \nDescription: Charity walk \nLocation: Piedmont Park Promenade \n*EVENT PENDING PERMIT*','Celeste Tennant \nctennant@parkinson.org \nDescription: Charity walk \nLocation: Piedmont Park Promenade \n*EVENT PENDING PERMIT*',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/city-permit-moving-day-atlanta-2',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:45','2019-09-21 01:17:45'),(1623,'2019 Pnc Atlanta 10 Miler &Amp; 5K','2019-pnc-atlanta-10-miler-amp-5k-october-20-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-10-20',NULL,'N/A','6:00 AM','10:00 AM','On Sunday, October 20th, starting at 6:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Volunteers needed! The Piedmont Park Conservancy has been invited to help cheer on runners at the PNC Atlanta 10 Miler &amp; 5K. Volunteers will help encourage runners as they pass through the Park. If you are interested in helping, email volunteers@piedmontpark.org.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/2019-pnc-atlanta-10-miler-5k',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:49','2019-09-21 01:17:49'),(1624,'Chc Fly K Fun Run','chc-fly-k-fun-run-october-20-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2019-10-20',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','11:00 AM','Michelle Hodgson \nmichelle@chcatlanta.org \nDescription: Exercise for families \nLocation: The Meadow Piedmont Park \n*EVENT PENDING PERMIT*','Michelle Hodgson \nmichelle@chcatlanta.org \nDescription: Exercise for families \nLocation: The Meadow Piedmont Park \n*EVENT PENDING PERMIT*',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://www.piedmontpark.org/event/chc-fly-k-fun-run',NULL,'2019-09-21 01:17:52','2019-09-21 01:17:52'),(1625,'Little Hands...big Lovefest!','little-handsbig-lovefest-october-20-2019-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,