t-miller-tickets-142546870527',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:02:34','2021-04-10 01:02:34'),(2636,'Clark Beckham','clark-beckham-december-1-2021-music-eddies-attic',7,1,1,2,'2021-12-01',NULL,'$15 - $50','7:00 PM','10:00 PM','See live music at Eddie\'s Attic on Wednesday, December 1st. Starting at 7:00 PM, with bands including Clark Beckham.','',0,1,'provider',0,0,0,'https://www.eventbrite.com/e/clark-beckham-tickets-149483277507',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:02:37','2021-04-10 01:02:37'),(2637,'Green Market (A Local Farmers Market)','green-market-a-local-farmers-market-april-10-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-10',NULL,'N/A','9:00 AM','1:00 PM','On Saturday, April 10th, starting at 9:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Voted one of the top five farmer\'s markets in Atlanta byAccess Atlanta, Green Market encourages sustainable communities in the most basic way - by providing shoppers with direct access to local farmers and small businesses. Come walk the market and enjoy the fun every Saturday from 9 am - 1 pm, March - November. \nEnjoy local farmers, bakers, jams, preserves and artisan goods. There is something for everyone. While you shop, you can enjoy prepared foods and drinks for breakfast and lunch. \nThe Green Market is following CDC protocols and requires all customers to wear masks and socially distance. \nGreen Market Webpage',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/green-market-a-local-farmers-market/2021-04-10',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:20','2021-04-10 01:04:20'),(2638,'Piedmont Park Guided History Tour','piedmont-park-guided-history-tour-april-10-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-10',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','11:30 PM','On Saturday, April 10th, starting at 10:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','The Piedmont Park History Walking Tours include an introduction to the park\'s vibrant past and present. Walk with us and discover how Piedmont Park\'s rich history is undeniably intertwined with the development of Atlanta. Together, we\'ll explore the fascinating historical and physical evolution of iconic Piedmont Park from forest to farm to fairgrounds for the Piedmont Exposition of 1887 and the Cotton States and International Exposition of 1895, to Atlanta\'s premier urban green space. \n\nLed by docent volunteers\nFree and open to all ages\nPlease wear appropriate clothing for the weather as the tour is outside and involves walking\n10 am; 60 - 90 minutes in length\nMeet atGreen Marketand Conservancy information table located at 12th St. and Piedmont Ave. NE Park entrance\n\n*Please note that reservations are required- sign uphere. History tours are available on a first come, first serve basis.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/piedmont-park-guided-history-tour/2021-04-10',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:26','2021-04-10 01:04:26'),(2639,'Kinetics And Learn','kinetics-and-learn-april-14-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-14',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','12:30 PM','On Wednesday, April 14th, starting at 10:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','The Conservancy\'s Education team is partnering with fitness expert Saidah Jones, CSCS to offer this program series. This opportunity offers an awesome learning experience in the Park while also filling a need for parents in their effort to keep their kids active and moving during virtual school. Saidah will be providing the physical education portion (\"Kinetics\") and the Education team will be providing a hands-on STEM based learning opportunity (\"Learn\"). \nOur Kinetics and Learn programs are designed for K-3 grade. \n\nPlease note- masks are required in this program. \n10:00am-12:15pm\n$40 per session\n\n \nSign up here: https://anc.apm.activecommunities.com/piedmontpark/activity/search?activity_select_param=2&amp;viewMode=list',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/kinetics-and-learn/2021-04-14',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:29','2021-04-10 01:04:29'),(2640,'Green Market (A Local Farmers Market)','green-market-a-local-farmers-market-april-17-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-17',NULL,'N/A','9:00 AM','1:00 PM','On Saturday, April 17th, starting at 9:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Voted one of the top five farmer\'s markets in Atlanta byAccess Atlanta, Green Market encourages sustainable communities in the most basic way - by providing shoppers with direct access to local farmers and small businesses. Come walk the market and enjoy the fun every Saturday from 9 am - 1 pm, March - November. \nEnjoy local farmers, bakers, jams, preserves and artisan goods. There is something for everyone. While you shop, you can enjoy prepared foods and drinks for breakfast and lunch. \nThe Green Market is following CDC protocols and requires all customers to wear masks and socially distance. \nGreen Market Webpage',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/green-market-a-local-farmers-market/2021-04-17',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:33','2021-04-10 01:04:33'),(2641,'Piedmont Park Guided History Tour','piedmont-park-guided-history-tour-april-17-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-17',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','11:30 PM','On Saturday, April 17th, starting at 10:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','The Piedmont Park History Walking Tours include an introduction to the park\'s vibrant past and present. Walk with us and discover how Piedmont Park\'s rich history is undeniably intertwined with the development of Atlanta. Together, we\'ll explore the fascinating historical and physical evolution of iconic Piedmont Park from forest to farm to fairgrounds for the Piedmont Exposition of 1887 and the Cotton States and International Exposition of 1895, to Atlanta\'s premier urban green space. \n\nLed by docent volunteers\nFree and open to all ages\nPlease wear appropriate clothing for the weather as the tour is outside and involves walking\n10 am; 60 - 90 minutes in length\nMeet atGreen Marketand Conservancy information table located at 12th St. and Piedmont Ave. NE Park entrance\n\n*Please note that reservations are required- sign uphere. History tours are available on a first come, first serve basis.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/piedmont-park-guided-history-tour/2021-04-17',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:36','2021-04-10 01:04:36'),(2642,'Virtual: Olmsted And America\'s Urban Parks Watch Party And Panel Discussion Event','virtual-olmsted-and-americas-urban-parks-watch-party-and-panel-discussion-event-april-24-2021-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2021-04-24','2021-04-26','N/A','8:00 AM','6:30 PM','On Saturday, April 24th, starting at 8:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Piedmont Park Conservancy is a proud partner of the national Olmsted 200 Bicentennial Celebration. Olmsted 200 invites you to screen Olmsted and America\'s Urban Parks, a documentary narrated by actress Kerry Washington, for free and at your convenienceApril 24-25, and then join other FLO fans for a live panel discussion onApril 26 from 5:30 pm - 6:30 pm ETabout the many ways Olmsted\'s values influence American life today. \nModerated byJustin Worland,TIMEMagazine\'s senior climate correspondent, the panel brings together a diverse group of thought leaders to examine how Olmsted\'s parks and visionary ideas continue to shape communities across the country. Panelists include: \n\nDr. Thaisa Way,Program Director for Garden &amp; Landscape Studies at Dumbarton Oaks Research Library and Collection\nHappy Haynes,Executive Director of Denver Parks and Recreation\nJustin DiBerardinis, FDR Park Director, Philadelphia Parks and Recreation\n\nRegistertoday for this exclusive virtual event. Once registered, you will receive a link to watch the film and join the party onApril 26 from 5:30 - 6:30 pm ET.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/virtual-olmsted-and-americas-urban-parks-watch-party-and-panel-discussion-event',NULL,'2021-04-10 01:04:40','2021-04-10 01:04:40'),(2643,'Green Market (A Local Farmers Marke