y, February 24th. Starting at 9:15 PM, with bands including Lucky Duck.','',0,1,'provider',0,0,0,'https://link.dice.fm/aa85de46b325',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:27:59','2026-02-20 01:27:59'),(2940,'February Fun Camp 2026','february-fun-camp-2026-february-19-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-19',NULL,'N/A','9:00 AM','4:00 PM','On Thursday, February 19th, starting at 9:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join Piedmont Park Conservancy for our February Fun camp! We\'ll spend the week of February 16-20 playing outside, participating in STEAM-focused activities, and learning about the plants and animals that call the Park home. This program is designed for students in grades K-5. Please pack two snacks, a lunch, and a water bottle. Drop off: 8:30-9:00am Program: 9:00am-4:00pm Pickup: 4:00pm-4:30pm.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/february-fun-camp-2026/2026-02-19',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:08','2026-02-20 01:28:08'),(2941,'Figure Drawing - 2/19','figure-drawing-219-february-19-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-19',NULL,'N/A','7:00 PM','9:00 PM','On Thursday, February 19th, starting at 7:00 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join Piedmont Park Conservancy as we host monthly Figure Drawing Sessions! We will start at 7PM and end at 9PM.Practice your creativity with Piedmont Park Conservancy during our monthly Figure Drawing session! Please plan to bring your own materials. This will feature a live model and include shorter gesture poses as well as longer poses. This is self-directed practice with no formal instruction provided.Pre-registration required for each session. 10 registrants minimum required for program to run. Reach out to programs@piedmontpark.org for information/assistance with booking this program as a group activity, or for information on financial assistance.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/figure-drawing-2-19',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:11','2026-02-20 01:28:11'),(2942,'February Fun Camp 2026','february-fun-camp-2026-february-20-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-20',NULL,'N/A','9:00 AM','4:00 PM','On Friday, February 20th, starting at 9:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join Piedmont Park Conservancy for our February Fun camp! We\'ll spend the week of February 16-20 playing outside, participating in STEAM-focused activities, and learning about the plants and animals that call the Park home. This program is designed for students in grades K-5. Please pack two snacks, a lunch, and a water bottle. Drop off: 8:30-9:00am Program: 9:00am-4:00pm Pickup: 4:00pm-4:30pm.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/february-fun-camp-2026/2026-02-20',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:14','2026-02-20 01:28:14'),(2943,'Weekly Walking Club','weekly-walking-club-february-24-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-24',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','10:45 AM','On Tuesday, February 24th, starting at 10:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join the Conservancy and fellow park fans for a weekly group walk in Piedmont Park! \nEvery Tuesday, we host a 45-minute walk on Tuesdays at 10am. Each walk will feature different popular paths while answering any questions you may have about Piedmont Park or the Conservancy. \nFor questions, please contact Kaycee Walker at programs@piedmontpark.org. \nMeet in front of Dockside near the 12th gate entrance, five minutes prior to departure. Walk up, no RSVP required.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/weekly-walking-club-3/2026-02-24',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:16','2026-02-20 01:28:16'),(2944,'Community Game Night, Free Community Program!','community-game-night-free-community-program-february-24-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-24',NULL,'Free','6:00 PM','8:00 PM','On Tuesday, February 24th, starting at 6:00 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Whether you\'ve never cracked open a mah jongg set, want to sharpen your chess openings, or have a game box collecting dust on the shelf.... this is your chance to come together and play! Experienced players are encouraged to join in, share tips, and help newcomers discover the joy of a good game night. We will have various games available.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/community-game-night-free-community-program',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:19','2026-02-20 01:28:19'),(2945,'Connect And Learn: Space Travel With Chris Thompson','connect-and-learn-space-travel-with-chris-thompson-february-25-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-02-25',NULL,'Free','6:00 PM','7:30 PM','On Wednesday, February 25th, starting at 6:00 PM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join Chris Thompson, president of the GA Meteorite Association, as he dives into space travel and Artemis missions! You\'ll also get to check out lunar meteorites! This free event is designed to connect folks who are solar system curious or serious. Chris will present for an hour, then we will have time for Q&A.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/connect-and-learn-space-travel-with-chris-thompson-2',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:21','2026-02-20 01:28:24'),(2946,'Weekly Walking Club','weekly-walking-club-march-3-2026-other-piedmont-park',8,1,5,2,'2026-03-03',NULL,'N/A','10:00 AM','10:45 AM','On Tuesday, March 3rd, starting at 10:00 AM. Go check out this event at Piedmont Park!','Join the Conservancy and fellow park fans for a weekly group walk in Piedmont Park! \nEvery Tuesday, we host a 45-minute walk on Tuesdays at 10am. Each walk will feature different popular paths while answering any questions you may have about Piedmont Park or the Conservancy. \nFor questions, please contact Kaycee Walker at programs@piedmontpark.org. \nMeet in front of Dockside near the 12th gate entrance, five minutes prior to departure. Walk up, no RSVP required.',0,1,'provider',0,1,0,'https://piedmontpark.org/event/weekly-walking-club-3/2026-03-03',NULL,'2026-02-20 01:28:24','2026-02-20 01:28:24'),(2947,'Crochet Worksho